Package: parkeze-usb-cellular
Depends: parkeze-base, parkeze-cellular
Maintainer: Joseph Telaak <joseph@parkeze.com>
Architecture: all
Description: A USB cellular adapter that is an Ethernet device, as an uplink.
 Brings a HiLink dongle or a tethered phone up as usbwan, a DHCP client that
 every Parkeze script treats as cellular: billed, kept from the management
 tunnel and, when the site says so, from LoRaWAN uplinks.
 .
 The kernel modules and usb-modeswitch are not dependencies: they are per
 target, and PACKAGES_USB_CELLULAR in boards/common/board.conf installs them
 alongside this on the boards with a USB host port to plug one into.
